<article class="entry" id="medmnist">
  <span class="tag">Fellowship project</span>
  <h3>Explainability of tree based ensembles for medical image classification</h3>
  <p class="meta"><span class="venue">IASc–INSA–NASI Summer Research Fellowship 2025</span> &nbsp;·&nbsp; Guide: Dr. Srikrishnan Divakaran, Krea University</p>
  <figure class="fig" data-fig>
    {% include "figures/medmnist.svg" %}
    <figcaption>Real MedMNIST test images, routed one modality at a time: the parent forest picks the modality, the matching expert makes the call, and the right panel shows that modality's result and explanation. The chest X ray importance map was recomputed for this page from a random forest on PneumoniaMNIST (test AUC 0.94).</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <ul class="metrics">
    <li><span class="v">98.7%</span><span class="k">modality routing accuracy</span></li>
    <li><span class="v">0.95 / 0.91</span><span class="k">AUC, pneumonia / breast</span></li>
    <li><span class="v">&lt;0.01 s</span><span class="k">inference per image, CPU</span></li>
